  "_doc": "Lead SNPs from Shaffer et al. 2016 (PLoS Genet 12(8):e1006149) S1 Table (meta-analysis p<5e-7), one per trait, mapped to this project's measures. Only 5 of 14 reach genome-wide significance (p<5e-8); the rest are suggestive.",
  "_honesty": "Verbatim from S1: rsid, effect_allele (minor allele), maf, beta_mm, se (Pittsburgh sample), P_meta. DERIVED, not published: var_explained = (beta/se)^2/N. It comes from the discovery sample and is selected on significance, so it is an UPPER BOUND (winner's curse); true effects are likely smaller. Measure definitions only approximate Shaffer's (S5): right-side landmarks instead of left, alare instead of alar-curvature point for nasal ala length. These loci affect the synthetic MEASUREMENT phenotype only; the shape target beta is untouched. Nothing here is a finding about real faces.",
